Standard MC simulation for an ion in a non-aqueous solvent:

The ion is specified in ionzmat and the solvent, T and P in ionpar.
ionzmat currently contains Sr++, and zmatBa is for Ba++, and the
designated solvent is THF. Other possibilities are:
CH3OH, CH3CN, MEOME, C3H8, ARGON, MECL2, CHCL3, CCL4, DMSO, or OTHER
if using a custom solvent (see the user's manual).
The command file ioncmd or ion.bat (Windows) is set up to
run 2M configurations of equilibration and 4M configurations of averaging.

to execute, then
for Linux/UNIX -
csh ioncmd >& log &

for Windows -
ion

Time Required: 45 minutes on a 2.4 GHz Pentium

For a related review, see: KM Fromm & ED Gueneau, Polyhedron
23 (2004) 1479-1504.
